Result magnetic powers encode walk profiles:
    Attribution: magnetic2025; Supplement S.II, Theorem 1; adapted; scope: forward transform
    Let n: Natural
    Assume positive: n > 0
    Let A be a real n×n matrix
    Let m: Natural
    Let q be a real number
    Let M = magnetic matrix(A,q)
    Conclude: matrix power(M,m) = walk Fourier sum(A,m,q)

Result size specific Cheeger inequality:
    Attribution: cheeger2026; Theorem 3.1; adapted; scope: connected simple graphs and positive mu
    Let n: Natural
    Let G: Graph(n)
    Let μ be a real number
    Assume connectivity: connected(G)
    Assume nontrivial: n ≥ 2
    Assume range: 0 < μ and μ ≤ 1/2
    Assume admissibility: admissible size(G,μ)
    Let φ = conductance(G,μ)
    Let ψ = ordinary conductance(G)
    Let spectral = spectral minimum(G,μ)
    Let t = μ^2/(μ^2 + 1/2 - μ)
    Conclude:
        ((t*φ + (1-t)*ψ)^2)/4 ≤ spectral
        and
        spectral ≤ 2*φ

Result trace bound gives a suboptimality certificate:
    Attribution: sdplr2026; Corollary 2, equation (3); adapted; scope: symmetric coefficient representation of the measurement map
    Let n, m: Natural
    Assume dimensions: n > 0 and m > 0
    Let C, X, Z be real n×n matrices
    Let B: Measurements(n,m)
    Let b, y be real m-vectors
    Let α be a real number
    Assume cost: symmetric(C)
    Assume measurements: symmetric measurements(B)
    Assume bound: α ≥ 0
    Assume candidate: feasible(B,b,α,X)
    Assume optimizer: minimizer(C,B,b,α,Z)
    Let d = dual bound(C,B,b,y,α)
    Conclude: matrix inner product(C,X) - matrix inner product(C,Z) ≤ matrix inner product(C,X) - d

